    "created_at": "2023-05-08T22:44:43Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-05-08T22:44:43Z",
    "body": "I think that depends, doesn't it? If they click somewhere near the top of the page, then press tab, they probably want to focus the next sequential-focusable one after that click point, i.e. something close by, probably still near the top. But if they click somewhere near the bottom of the page, then pressing tab to focus the browser UI makes sense, since the browser UI is always \"between\" the bottom of the page and the top of the page in the tab cycle.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
