    "created_at": "2023-06-19T16:34:34Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-06-19T16:34:34Z",
    "body": "What @domenic suggests makes sense to me. There's no reason for focus to go backwards and we don't have a special \"don't go via browser UI\" heuristic (although browsers are allowed to offer that of course).\r\n\r\n(Unfortunately the clicking doesn't work as expected, e.g., if I click between the controls on `data:text/html,<p><input><p><input>` the first one seems to always get focused afterwards. But that's a general thing some browsers have, search-in-page also frequently goes from the top despite that not always being the most useful behavior.)\r\n\r\ncc @rniwa ",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
