    "created_at": "2023-07-19T20:23:30Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-07-19T20:23:30Z",
    "body": "I agree with what @domenic suggests also. From a user's perspective, if they click near the bottom of the document, the focus should move to something after (below) that point. If there are no further tab stops, the expectation would be that it \"wraps around\" to the browser UI.\r\n\r\n(What's really unfortunate is that users likely also expect this when clicking in the `<body>` but at a pixel location below any DOM content. In that case, it'd also make sense to go to the browser UI. But the focus traversal doesn't (and likely can't) take that into account.)",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
